Review the following TypeScript retry helper and provide corrected implementation-ready code plus tests:

async function retry<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>, attempts = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= attempts; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); } catch (error) {
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100 * 2 ** i));
    }
  }
}

The corrected design must preserve the final error, avoid an extra attempt, support cancellation, and avoid sleeping after the final failure.
